# WolkaraForever layer patch 0036 - profile: copy the store the released client uses
#
# Why: the installer copied `Data` wholesale. `Data` holds the CASC store every
# product in one installation shares plus a per-product index folder; a beta's
# `wow_classic_beta` folder left behind (or on the Mac) belongs to a build that is
# not being installed, and copying it into the app's store would mix two builds'
# indexes. It now copies the shared store and the product's own folder, which
# `.flavor.info` names. The release also ships a `Helpers` folder (a voice proxy
# helper) beside the client's `Resources`, and both are copied.
#
# History: this patch also moved the profile from the beta (`_classic_beta_`,
# `World of Warcraft Beta.app`) to the released game (`_forever_`,
# `World of Warcraft.app`, product `wowf`). Tolkara edc3628 made that move itself,
# with a build_info check of its own, so only the installer's `Data` selection, the
# `Helpers` copy and the README's description of them are left here.
#
# Applies to: profiles/wow-forever/{install.py,README.md}.
# Upstream: candidate.
#
